<p>Dear Google Drive User,</p>

<p>We are writing to let you know that starting <strong>October 13, 2020</s=
trong>, Google Drive is making a change so that its trash behaves more cons=
istently with the rest of Google applications (such as Gmail) with regards =
to automatic deletion. This means that <strong>any file that is put into <a=
 href=3Dhttps://www.google.com/appserve/mkt/p/AD-FnEzwwdi7ud4I4SkQkFKkS5fiX=
32NmKN6O1fqJzN00shYPSVDxhHM6WEmcX-78I-XycdcJJydgx12Jn77ygSYhuX49DdE3BS90hE =
target=3D_blank>Google Drive=E2=80=99s =E2=80=98My Drive=E2=80=99 trash</a>=
 will begin to be automatically deleted after 30 consecutive days in the tr=
ash</strong>. Items in trash will still continue to consume quota and your =
storage will still continue to be shared across Google Drive, Gmail, and Go=
ogle Photos.</p>

<p>Please note that starting October 13, 2020, any files already in a user=
=E2=80=99s trash, will remain there for 30 days. After the 30-day-period <s=
trong>files that have been in the trash for longer than 30 days will begin =
to be automatically deleted.</strong></p>

<h3>What does this mean for me?</h3>

<p>Any file that has been in the <a href=3Dhttps://www.google.com/appserve/=
mkt/p/AD-FnEzwwdi7ud4I4SkQkFKkS5fiX32NmKN6O1fqJzN00shYPSVDxhHM6WEmcX-78I-Xy=
cdcJJydgx12Jn77ygSYhuX49DdE3BS90hE target=3D_blank>Google Drive trash</a> f=
or longer than 30 days after <strong>October 13, 2020</strong> will be auto=
matically deleted forever, <strong>regardless of whether or not you have ac=
knowledged any in-app messaging</strong>. We will be showing in-app messagi=
ng in Drive starting September 15, 2020 and in our Editors products (such a=
s Google Docs and Google Forms) starting September 29, 2020.</p>

<p>A few things to note:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Files in <a href=3Dhttps://www.google.com/appserve/mkt/p/AD-FnEz5khU3=
gCzQ_2CcoaYr216UWw9EO7Ry1pjJ7xN2ww7v1G_8TNpPFYQD-GugxkBaD60f_FsftpNUufWnIZX=
C-9SViNYK4SyhHZXiOYCv0hH5wnEs8JGD target=3D_blank>shared drives</a> trash a=
re already <a href=3Dhttps://www.google.com/appserve/mkt/p/AD-FnExn0isIgLpO=
BkICQSuNAHmLX_LnjCe3_VnL5RJSq08lD9dA4PMbGey6WOdCau5dkebS1k-h-d7w6Ci2jQR-wgh=
DI6x4YQatAlpF2H_vRtoT target=3D_blank>automatically deleted</a> after 30 da=
ys.</li>
  <li>These changes affect items that are trashed from any device and any p=
latform.</li>
  <li>There is no impact to Backup and Sync behavior.</li>
</ul>

<h3>What do I need to do?</h3>

<ul>
  <li>You can always <a href=3Dhttps://www.google.com/appserve/mkt/p/AD-FnE=
x3LCJFAkyVNmf2NZw5DA3aqi5ogIxqbF4t1EXZwcZfk9GiAxi2BwNGzuyWsKgBPd5RXs-amwrvU=
RxrNQ1IGVdC8zL06U2-foWOgx3K9QOmZ89z-g target=3D_blank>restore</a> files fro=
m trash before the 30 day time window.</li>
  <li>If you are using Google Drive on Android or iOS, please <strong>updat=
e to the latest versions</strong> so you can be updated on the most recent =
in-app notifications.</li>
</ul>

<p>Sincerely,</p>

<p>Google Drive team</p>

